{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Ticket 3 (beaming-snively-urial) plan-review surfaced a deeper problem than a wrong test path: aggregate_findings has NO live caller in src/ per the reviewer -- superseded by ADR 0075 (retire single-pass code-review route). My epic's premise for this specific consumer (aggregate.py picks the highest-severity representative) may target dead code, or the wrong function for the CURRENT four-pass pipeline's actual dedup mechanism. Spawned research to find: (1) what ADR 0075 actually retired, (2) confirm aggregate_findings has zero production callers, (3) find the CURRENT pipeline's real cross-finding dedup/ranking function and what field it ranks by. Holding ticket 3 revisions until this lands -- do not want to re-review a plan built on a wrong premise a third time."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788128278206801972,"uuid":"5a66e1d2-e400-4a46-94ac-d4d93a185b95"}